WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.560
Tealy here. Every sentence in a passage has a job.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.440
And test questions love to ask what that job is.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.140
Mostly, sentences do four jobs.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.880
They introduce a claim.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.380
They give evidence.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.320
They admit a limitation.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.440
Or they contrast ideas.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.260
Here's a report.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.060
A new fertilizer may help tomatoes grow.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.260
Treated plants grew taller than untreated ones.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.180
However, only six plants were tested.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.880
First sentence: that's the claim.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.860
Second: that's the evidence.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.220
Third: only six plants.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.560
That's a limitation.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.200
Its job is to say:

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.520
don't get too excited.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.940
Your turn. Trees can cool city streets.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.500
In one study,

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.360
shaded streets were three degrees cooler.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.720
What's the job of the second sentence?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.120
Go.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.040
Evidence! It backs up the claim.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:04.580
The fast way:

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:05.720
label as you read.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.940
Claim. Evidence. Limitation.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.800
Just little arrows in your head.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.820
But a limitation doesn't overturn the result.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.960
It doesn't say the fertilizer failed.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.140
So avoid answers that exaggerate the disagreement.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.940
And explain why the sentence is there,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.800
not just what topic it mentions.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:26.560
Now hit Try this skill!
